      "body": "NACK 5bdc91ee47c7aa510c0e1d8eb6a1d5de414de445\r\n\r\nI was surprised to find out that there was something I hadn't extracted from the BIP for `bdk-sp` implementation, but after doing some digging, I found the possible origin of its introduction:\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/1458#discussion_r1230292341\r\n\r\nIn that comment thread, _@josibake concluded to **not include** `sprt` in the BIP spec, although `bitcoin-core` silent payments PR from that moment did, as well as the recently merged bitcoin/bitcoin#35301 does.\r\n\r\nThe crux of the issue is in bitcoin/bitcoin#12314, where you can get an overview of the reasons for and against doing it.\r\n\r\nTechnically, the removal of `sprt` would be beneficial for `bdk-sp`, as the non binary distinction of the network introduced some bugs in the past: https://github.com/bitcoindevkit/bdk-sp/pull/70, but I consider https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/pull/1458#discussion_r1230292341 enough of an answer to keep the BIP as it is, and wait for bitcoin/bitcoin#12314 to be fixed (if ever), to reconsider this stance.\r\n\r\nThanks for refreshing me this!",
